# Functions

Functions are declared using the `func` keyword. Functions need to declare the types of all their arguments and return values.
As in the Python or Go programming languages, types are declared after the names of the arguments. When consecutive parameters share the same type, they can be grouped together (like `a` and `b`).

In the example, `mulAdd` takes three arguments: `x` of type `float32`, and `a` and `b`, both of type `[2][3]float32`. It returns a single value of type `[2][3]float32`.

